 its\n  stdout/exit never reach the gate command).\n- **NO-GO fallback (recorded):** if Foreman-substrate hosting fails the spike, validators run as a standalone\n  Node process Foreman shells to via `test-command` â€” same TAP contract.\n\n## Wave 2 â€” Eval harness: three validators as TAP emitters (P0.A R6/FIX-1/FIX-4/FIX-16â€²)\n**done-when:** one harness exposes three pluggable validators â€” (i) schema+path-existence, (ii) deterministic\ncanary eval, (iii) numeric-tolerance grader (calls a pure offline reference fn) â€” each emitting TAP, with the\nadvisory cross-family judge isolated (FIX-15) so its exit/stdout never reach the gate; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** an artifact with a missing referenced path, **When** validator (i) runs, **Then** it emits `not ok`\n  naming the missing path.\n- **Given** a deterministic canary run twice on identical input, **When** validator (ii) runs, **Then** it emits\n  byte-identical TAP both times (no non-determinism in the GATE path).\n- **Given** an unreachable advisory cross-family host, **When** the wave gate runs, **Then** the gate is GREEN\n  and a \"degraded-coverage\" advisory report is written (failure swallowed; FIX-15).\n\n## Wave 3 â€” Machine-checkable handoff-contract gate (P0.B NS5)\n**done-when:** a contract validator gates a stage handoff on schema-valid + all artifact_refs resolve on disk\n+ north_star round-trips byte-identical + open_questions empty; wired so Anchor's HANDOFF.md/NEXT-PROMPT.md and\nCrucible's locate-plan path both emit/validate it; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** a handoff doc whose `north_star` differs by one byte from the upstream, **When** the gate runs,\n  **Then** it emits `not ok` (round-trip failure).\n- **Given** a handoff doc with a non-empty `open_questions`, **When** the gate runs, **Then** it emits `not ok`\n  (blocks under-specified handoff).\n\n## Wave 4 â€” Skill-repo templates + tierâ†’model table + swap test (P0.C NS3/NS4/FIX-5)\n**done-when:** the per-skill repo skeleton (NORTH-STAR.md with non-goals as negative tests, SKILL.md,\nreferences/, LESSONS.md, journal/, CHANGELOG.md) + the net-new logical-tierâ†’model config table exist; a swap\ntest proves swapping the table changes the resolved model with zero skill-prose edits; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** the tierâ†’model table mapping `topâ†’A`, **When** the table is swapped to `topâ†’B` and a persona\n  resolves its model, **Then** the resolved model changes Aâ†’B and no SKILL.md byte changed.\n- **Note:** the swap test pins a model-respecting backend (gemini-cli driver), since the default Claude backend\n  ignores `opts.model` â€” else the test would pass vacuously.\n\n## Wave 5 â€” Journal 7-field schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop (P0.D NS1/NS2/NS3/R5)\n**done-when:** the 7-field journal schema + the sleep meta-recipe (cluster â†’ cross-context-corroborated distill\nâ†’ North-Star gate â†’ eval gate â†’ versioned promote with git rollback) exist and are TAP-tested on FIXTURE\njournals (real skills do not exist yet); `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** fixture journal entries where a candidate lesson advances a machine-checkable non-goal, **When** the\n  sleep loop runs, **Then** that lesson is REJECTED (North-Star gate) and logged, not promoted.\n- **Given** a candidate revision that regresses a frozen fixture canary, **When** the eval gate runs, **Then**\n  promotion is blocked and the prior version is retained (rollback).\n- **Given** a candidate lesson corroborated only by same-context repetition, **When** distillation runs, **Then**\n  it is NOT shipped (requires cross-context corroboration, R5).\n\n## Wave 6 â€” Foundry governance wiring + canary versioning + citation hygiene (P0.E/P0.F FIX-6/R7)\n**done-when:** map.json records canary SETS + templates as data/refs (Foundry stays stateless); the drift\nchecker + foundry invariant pytest stay GREEN; canary sets are versioned with skills (append-only; deletion =\nhuman call); SkillsBenchâ†’2602.12670 corrected and MemoryGraft dropped in carried docs; `node --test test/` GREEN.\n- **Given** a sleep cycle proposing a canary deletion, **When** governance validates it, **Then** it is BLOCKED\n  as a human-call (append-only enforced).\n- **Given** the Foundry invariant suite, **When** it runs, **Then** it is GREEN (canary/template entries valid,\n  drift checker GREEN).\n\n---\n\n## Project DONE\nDONE = Wave 6 GREEN (orchestrator-run `node --test test/`). At that point the shared substrate exists and is\nproven on fixtures: the deterministic eval harness (3 validators), the machine-checkable handoff contract, the\nper-skill repo templates + swappable tierâ†’model seam, the journal schema + North-Star-gated sleep loop with\nrollback, and the Foundry governance wiring. The cognitive-skill cycles, the recreate-a-paper proof, and the\nNS1 demonstration (each its own researchPrimeâ†’Crucibleâ†’Foreman cycle) build ON this substrate next â€” see\n`crucible/PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md`.\n","numLines":103,"startLine":1,"totalLines":103}}}
