{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BBkzoRH7tBrpPZFRYb439Z","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Portfolio Program â€” Sequence (the uber plan: cycles, not one build)\n2\t\n3\t> This is the program-level \"uber plan.\" It sequences the whole effort as a substrate build followed by a\n4\t> series of **per-skill cycles**, each of which is its OWN researchPrime deep-dive â†’ skill Crucible â†’ Foreman\n5\t> â†’ Learn. The per-skill METHOD (what makes the skill best-in-class) is produced inside each cycle's research +\n6\t> Crucible â€” NOT in this document and NOT in the Phase-0 infra plan. This restores the original cadence:\n7\t> \"multiple waves of researchPrime deep-dives + crucible specific for each wave, with a foreman follow on.\"\n8\t\n9\t## Why cycles, not one monolithic build\n10\tA structural done-floor (â‰¥3 non-goals, â‰¥K canaries, gates green) produces a GENERIC skill. What makes Gandalf\n11\ta genuinely useful critical-review tool â€” or Ramanujan a genuinely useful math-understanding tool â€” is its\n12\tMETHOD: the best-in-class techniques it embodies. That method must be researched and forged per skill, before\n13\tits protocol and canaries can be written (you cannot author good Gandalf canaries before you know what expert\n14\tcritical review actually does). Hence: one cycle per skill.\n15\t\n16\t## The per-skill cycle TEMPLATE (every skill runs this)\n17\t1. **researchPrime deep-dive** (stakes-scaled, evidence-laddered) on: \"best-in-class METHOD for <skill domain> â€”\n18\t   named frameworks/techniques/reference practitioners; failure modes; what separates expert from novice; how\n19\t   to encode it as a stateless SKILL.md protocol.\" Output â†’ the skill's research deliverable.\n20\t2. **Skill Crucible** (Stage 0â†’1â†’2, Shark-vetted): forge the skill's locked NORTH-STAR (purpose + machine-\n21\t   checkable non-goals + invariants), the SKILL.md PROTOCOL (the method), the persona/model-tier, the canary\n22\t   set (core + discriminating negative canaries, FIX-17â€²), and the journal/improvement protocol. Emits a\n23\t   Foreman-ready handoff for the skill, gated by Phase-0 infra.\n24\t3. **Foreman build**: build the skill to the per-skill done-floor (Master Plan), using the Phase-0 eval harness,\n25\t   templates, journal schema, and handoff contract.\n26\t   - **LESSON (Gandalf cycle, 2026-06-21): the Crucible Implementation Plan MUST include an explicit\n27\t     \"author SKILL.md\" wave with its own done-when.** Gandalf's plan framed every wave's done-when around\n28\t     `node --test` canaries + seam CODE (correct for PRINCIPLE-D) but never made the stateless `SKILL.md`\n29\t     runtime protocol a deliverable â€” so Foreman built the engine + canary spine with NO SKILL.md (it built\n30\t     exactly what the done-whens demanded). The SKILL.md was authored by hand afterward. Every future skill's\n31\t     Stage-2 plan adds a wave whose done-when is: `SKILL.md` exists + a canary asserts it references each\n32\t     North-Star pillar + the output it describes conforms to the committed schema the canaries check.\n33\t4. **Review / Learn**: Gandalf-style critical review (once Gandalf exists; bootstrap with the cross-family\n34\t   advisory judge + human for Gandalf itself) + run on 2â€“3 real tasks + seed the journal from genuine runs.\n35\t\n36\t## Sequence (dependency-ordered)\n37\t\n38\t### Stage A â€” Phase-0 shared infrastructure  [Foreman-ready NOW]\n39\t`IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md` (6 waves). Build first; everything below depends on it.\n40\t\n41\t### Stage B â€” Cognitive-skill cycles (each = the template above)\n42\tOrdered so the recreate-a-paper proof's data flow is satisfied (understand â†’ lineage â†’ data â†’ code â†’ verify):\n43\t\n44\t1. **Gandalf â€” critical review.** First, because it is also the Review-stage engine for later cycles.\n45\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class critical analysis / red-teaming / analytic rigor â€” e.g. structured\n46\t     analytic techniques (Heuer, ACH), argument mapping, steelmanning, premortem, the discipline of \"what\n47\t     is actually going on here\"; failure modes (confirmation bias, motivated reasoning, sycophancy); how\n48\t     top-tier review differs from surface critique. Persona tier = Fable 5.\n49\t   - *Bootstrap note (A4):* Gandalf is gated by Phase-0 infra + a CROSS-FAMILY advisory judge + human review â€”\n50\t     NOT by itself.\n51\t2. **Ramanujan â€” math/algorithm understanding.** Emits the understandâ†’build firewall (pure, offline,\n52\t   deterministic reference fn + spec + unit tests) the proof depends on (FIX-8/18).\n53\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class mathematical exposition + algorithm comprehension â€” derivation-checking,\n54\t     worked-example pedagogy, the Feynman technique, proof verification, dimensional/sanity analysis; how to\n55\t     turn a paper's method prose into a verified, runnable reference. Persona tier = Fable 5 / Opus.\n56\t3. **Literature review** (augmented researchPrime). Upstream lineage/lit-review is load-bearing for paper-repro.\n57\t   - *Research framing:* systematic-review method, citation-lineage mining, recovering tacit knowledge from\n58\t     cited code; what a rigorous lit/lineage report contains. Persona tier = Opus.\n59\t4. **Data analysis** â€” find/clean/analyze/report.\n60\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class EDA, data cleaning/validation, result-comparison + plotting practice;\n61\t     reproducible data pipelines. Persona tier = Sonnetâ†’Opus.\n62\t5. **Analytic + ML code** â€” R/Matlab/Python; JAX/PyTorch.\n63\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class scientific/ML coding practice; satisfying a frozen firewall spec;\n64\t     dependency-aware modular generation. Persona tier = Opus.\n65\t6. **Code verification** (co-designed with #5).\n66\t   - *Research framing:* best-in-class code-fidelity verification â€” visual artifacts a human can review,\n67\t     chunked walkthroughs, executed-number checks bound to a verified module (FIX-8). Persona = Fable 5.\n68\t\n69\t### Stage C â€” recreate-a-paper proof cycle  [needs Stage B skills]\n70\tIts own researchPrime (paper-repro pipeline SOTA â€” already partly done in Phase-0 research) + Crucible +\n71\tForeman. Composes the Stage-B skills; required upstream lineage/lit-review; Assumptions Ledger; understandâ†’build\n72\tfirewall; executed numbers BOUND to Ramanujan's pure reference fn; context-isolated advisory grader. The PROOF:\n73\treproduce Gelman ANOVA, graded on the deterministic architecture/handoff done-check (NOT fidelity).\n74\t\n75\t### Stage D â€” NS1 self-improvement demonstration\n76\tInject a known defect (a seeded deterministic-canary regression) into a built skill; a real sleep cycle must\n77\tRECOVER it (regression-then-recovery) â€” a no-op cannot pass. The self-improving proof.\n78\t\n79\t### Later portfolio (own cycles, beyond this program's proof)\n80\tJumper (brainstorm), doc-writing, legal analysis, propose-extensions recipe, then the productivity/personal\n81\tstateful agents (model-agnostic; GWL/t2rs swap-in deferred â€” parallel track).\n82\t\n83\t## FOUNDATIONAL CAPABILITY â€” skill-to-skill composition (user, 2026-06-20)\n84\tThe portfolio is CORE skills + COMPOSITIONAL skills that CALL the base skills (a compositional skill must\n85\tNEVER rebuild a capability a core skill already provides â€” it invokes it). These compositional skills are\n86\tagent-like; the semantics don't matter, the capability does. This requires a **skill-composition / invocation\n87\tcontract** â€” how skill A invokes skill B, passes typed input, receives B's typed output, and composes it â€”\n88\twhich PAIRS with the machine-checkable handoff contract (Phase-0 P0.B). Add to Phase-0 infra: a\n89\t**skill-invocation convention** (on a sub-agent-capable host: spawn skill B as a sub-agent via the host's\n90\tSkill/Agent tools; on a degraded host: honest inline degraded run with B's own degraded stamp) + a typed\n91\tcompose contract. Enables recreate-a-paper, propose-extensions, AND the deferred advisor skill below. Relates\n92\tto the GWL harness (the eventual agentic runtime â€” parallel track) but a lighter Claude-Code-substrate\n93\tcomposition contract works NOW.\n94\t\n95\t## DEFERRED â€” the \"deep-think advisor / magic Gandalf\" as a COMPOSITIONAL skill\n96\tThe expanded vision (diagnose + SITUATE via researchPrime + ELEVATE via foresight + VETTED value-adding\n97\tsuggestions) is its OWN later cycle, NOT the core Gandalf. Reason (Stage-1 Shark Tank, 2026-06-20): SITUATE+\n98\tELEVATE are un-researched, overlap Crucible(Oranges)/Jumper(ideation)/researchPrime, and the \"vetted magic\"\n99\tmechanism has an unsolved tension (adversarial vetting as a kill-filter selects for safe-but-obvious). Correct\n100\tbuild: a compositional \"Gandalf-Advisor\" skill that COMPOSES Gandalf-core (diagnose) + researchPrime (situate)\n101\t+ Jumper (ideate) + a foresight pass, then synthesizes & RISK-LABELS (vetting = honest grounded/promising-\n102\tbut-unverified/refuted tag, only refuted dropped â€” NOT a kill-filter). Starts with its OWN researchPrime dive\n103\tinto the generative-and-vetted method. Depends on: core Gandalf + Jumper built, and the skill-composition\n104\tcontract above.\n105\t\n106\t## What stays fixed across all cycles (the substrate contract)\n107\tPhase-0 infra (Stage A) + the Master Plan design pillars + the per-skill done-floor + PRINCIPLE-D (deterministic\n108\tgate; advisory judging isolated) + the machine-checkable handoff contract. Each skill cycle inherits these; the\n109\tresearch + Crucible add the per-skill METHOD on top.\n110\t\n111\t## Trio audit â€” DONE (2026-06-20)\n112\tSee `TRIO-AUDIT.md`. Verdict: the trio is good-enough (NOT substantially improvable for its purpose); do not\n113\tdetour. Two cheap, transferable wins approved for application: **C3** (Crucible complexity-triage gate to\n114\tright-size the pipeline â€” compounds across skill cycles) and **F3** (Foreman bounded plan-amendment halt\n115\tsub-type). The other 7 audited gaps were academic/benchmark-chasing or already-covered.\n116\t\n117\t## REQUIREMENT â€” the trio self-improves too (user, 2026-06-20)\n118\tWhen the journaling + North-Star-gated sleep-improvement infra exists (Phase-0 Waves 5â€“6), the TRIO skills\n119\t(researchPrime / Crucible / Foreman) MUST be brought under it, exactly like the cognitive skills:\n120\t- Each gets a `NORTH-STAR.md` (formalize their purpose + machine-checkable non-goals), a `journal/`, `LESSONS.md`,\n121\t  and entry into the sleep loop.\n122\t- Their **canary set = their existing test suites + behavioral canaries** (e.g. Crucible locks North Star before\n123\t  Stage 1; Foreman HALTs on ambiguity; researchPrime stamps degraded mode). The no-regression gate for a trio\n124\t  sleep-revision is their own test suite staying GREEN.\n125\t- Sleep improves the SKILL.md protocol (engine changes allowed, gated by their tests), under the SAME anti-drift\n126\t  rule (a revision cannot drift the skill from its locked purpose).\n127\t- **Seed their first journals from real sessions** â€” incl. the 2026-06-20 program session (researchPrime caught\n128\t  its own citation errors; Crucible caught its own wrong fix FIX-16 + the breadth-first mis-reconciliation;\n129\t  the C3/F3 audit is the manual preview of what a trio sleep cycle would surface). Add a \"register trio under\n130\t  journaling/sleep\" step right after Phase-0 infra (Stage A+).\n131\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63322f7c-eeca-4ca2-a012-71bc44c711cb","uuid":"e127bb36-bb6d-475e-ae02-032905e60705","timestamp":"2026-06-23T00:48:34.770Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\planning\\portfolio-program\\crucible\\PROGRAM-SEQUENCE.md","content":"# Portfolio Program â€” Sequence (the uber plan: cycles, not one build)\n\n> This is the program-level \"uber plan.\" It sequences the whole effort as a substrate